# Pharmacy Patient Flow

## 0. Overview

This file is the direct Pharmacy flow source of truth for HOSSPI HMS. Pharmacy is an **executing department** — orders attach to **encounter_id**. Pharmacy dispenses; Nursing records administration (MAR) on IPD. Align with [`.cursor/flows/opd-flow.mdc`](./opd-flow.mdc), [`.cursor/flows/ipd-flow.mdc`](./ipd-flow.mdc), [`.cursor/flows/nursing-flow.mdc`](./nursing-flow.mdc), [`.cursor/flows/discharge-flow.mdc`](./discharge-flow.mdc), and [`.cursor/app-write-up.mdc`](../app-write-up.mdc).

## 1. Goal

Enable pharmacists to fulfill medication orders: billing gates, prepare and attest dispense, manage returns, maintain stock visibility, and support **discharge take-home medicines**.

### Central encounter rule

Pharmacy executes dispensing on encounter-linked orders. It does not create encounters or own MAR administration.

---

## 2. Position in the Patient Journey

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    OPD[OPD PHARMACY_REQUESTED] --> PHARM[Pharmacy workbench]
    IPD[IPD medication order §7] --> PHARM
    CLIN[Prescription dialog] --> PHARM
    PHARM --> DISP[Dispense attested]
    DISP --> OPD_DONE[OPD stage updated]
    DISP --> MAR[Nursing MAR — nursing-flow]
    IPD_DISC[discharge-flow §3 step 5] --> PHARM
```

| Source | Flow reference | Pharmacy responsibility |
| ------ | -------------- | ----------------------- |
| OPD | [opd-flow §3](./opd-flow.mdc) `PHARMACY_REQUESTED` | Outpatient dispense queue |
| IPD ward | [ipd-flow §7](./ipd-flow.mdc) medication route | Dispense → ward MAR (Nursing) |
| IPD discharge | [ipd-flow §10 step 5](./ipd-flow.mdc), [discharge-flow §3](./discharge-flow.mdc) | Take-home medicines; `Medication Pending` clearance |
| Billing | [ipd-flow §4](./ipd-flow.mdc) | Billing gate on orders; deferred on urgent admits |

---

## 3. Step-by-Step Pharmacy Workflow

| Step | Stage | What Happens | Main Role |
| ---- | ----- | ------------ | --------- |
| 1 | Order received | Pharmacy order on workbench (OPD or IPD). | System |
| 2 | Billing gate | Pay-now or bill-later via order billing payload. | Pharmacist / Cashier |
| 3 | Prepare dispense | Pick, label, verify against order. | Pharmacist |
| 4 | Attest dispense | Confirm dispense complete. | Pharmacist |
| 5 | Ward delivery / pickup | Medicine reaches patient; Nursing MAR. | Pharmacist / Nurse |
| 6 | Return (if applicable) | Process returns with reason. | Pharmacist |
| 7 | Discharge medicines | Take-home prep for [discharge-flow](./discharge-flow.mdc) clearance. | Pharmacist |

---

## 4. Backend Workbench Contract

Use pharmacy-workspace routes: workbench list, `prepare-dispense`, `attest-dispense`, cancel, return. Billing via order PUT with billing payload or integrated gate.

Queue scopes: distinguish **outpatient** vs **inpatient** vs **discharge-pending** when API supports filters.

---

## 5. Module Boundaries

| Own in Pharmacy | Do not duplicate |
| --------------- | -------------- |
| Dispensing, returns, stock visibility on workbench | Prescription creation (Clinical) |
| Billing gate on orders | Cashier reconciliation (Billing) |
| Take-home medicine prep | MAR administration (Nursing) |
| | OPD/IPD stage mutations |

